# Same range cuts as the DC3/DC4 sources (optimizes sim time):
DefaultRangeCut 0.005
Region Spacecraft
Spacecraft.Volume SCbody
Spacecraft.RangeCut 1.

Region Pipebody
Pipebody.Volume PIPbody
Pipebody.RangeCut 1.

DetectorTimeConstant 0.000002

# Local particle event: quasi-trapped electrons, exp(-E/100 keV),
# peak I(>30 keV) = 130 e/cm2/s/sr at 90 deg pitch, sin^4 pitch-angle distribution.
# Rocking -21.88 deg, yaw 58.18 deg, field dip 0 deg. Directions in detector frame.
DataChallenge.Source R1_LOCLPAR0040
R1_LOCLPAR0040.ParticleType 3
R1_LOCLPAR0040.Beam FarFieldNormalizedEnergyBeamFluxFunction R1_LOCLPAR0040_beam.dat
R1_LOCLPAR0040.Spectrum NormalizedEnergyBeamFluxFunction
# Light-curve times are relative to t_ref = 1835876880.0 (unix s, first orientation row of this burst).
# Simulate with DC3_final_530km_3_month_with_slew_15sbins_GalacticEarth_cut_normed.ori and add t_ref to the simulated times afterwards.
# Original light curve (absolute unix times): R1_LOCLPAR0040_lightcurve.dat; see sim_time_reference.txt.
R1_LOCLPAR0040.Lightcurve File false R1_LOCLPAR0040_lightcurve_shifted.dat
